---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About SCAN II</h1>
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The Project</h2>
      <p>
        The SCAN II Project is developed upon the results of the SCAN project and aims at contributing to
        the correct and coherent implementation of EU civil procedures in cross-border cases, enhancing
        access to justice through the further development of the SCAN e-platform and database.
      </p>

      <h2>Objectives</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Digitalization Support:</strong> Supporting the digitalization of cross-border enforcement
          of civil claims under the European Small Claims Procedure (ESCP) and European Order for Payment (EOP).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Platform Development:</strong> Further development of the SCAN e-platform providing
          comprehensive information on national enforcement procedures across EU Member States.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Research & Analysis:</strong> Conducting comparative and analytical studies of best practices
          for national enforcement authorities.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Network Building:</strong> Strengthening the network of academic experts and institutional
          partners working on EU civil justice.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>EU Funding</h2>
      <p>
        This project is co-funded by the European Union's Justice Programme (2021-2027). The content of this
        website represents the views of the author only and is their sole responsibility. The European Commission
        does not accept any responsibility for use that may be made of the information it contains.
      </p>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        The European Small Claims Procedure (ESCP) and the European Order for Payment (EOP) are EU civil
        procedures designed to simplify and speed up cross-border litigation for claims. However, the
        enforcement of judgments obtained through these procedures still relies on national enforcement systems,
        which vary significantly across EU Member States.
      </p>
      <p>
        The SCAN II project addresses these challenges by providing comprehensive information on enforcement
        procedures and promoting best practices across the European Union.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
